Larry Page reportedly has a number for how much computing will end up in space: five nines. As in 99.999%.

@patrick_oshag heard it secondhand: "Someone asked Larry Page how much of compute will be orbital, and he said five-nines."

@martin_casado's reason it might happen: "It's just basically regulatory." He thinks there are 500 proposed bills to stop data center building in the US, Texas included.

From @InvestLikeBest.
